1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,400
Oct 2026: resold Ledgers carried a hidden eSIM board
that leaked seed phrases.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,900
Genuine Check can't see it. A milligram scale can.

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:09,900
tamper-check: enter scale readings, get a verdict.
All numbers are simulated examples.

4
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,710
Weigh 3 times on a 0.001 g scale (re-zero between).
Type the readings.

5
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:17,210
Average +0.007 g vs the example reference 57.000 g.
Inside ±0.050 g → LIKELY GENUINE, risk 0.

6
00:00:17,410 --> 00:00:21,210
+1.2 g, plus cellular bursts every ~30 s while OFF
in a Faraday bag → TAMPERED, risk 100.

7
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:24,210
Red = suspected added mass. Rings = radio bursts.

8
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:28,050
A reopened, re-glued case: type the readings.

9
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:31,550
+0.359 g: over 2× the tolerance.
Too light for a board, but it was opened → SUSPICIOUS.

10
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:34,550
Green = expected center of mass, yellow = measured.

11
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:36,950
Same tampered unit on a 1 g kitchen scale: 57, 57, 57.

12
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:40,450
0.3 g rounds away → missed.
The tool warns: 1 g scales are demo-only.

13
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:44,340
Same unit on a 0.001 g scale.

14
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:47,340
+0.312 g caught → SUSPICIOUS, risk 50.

15
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:51,340
Flagged: don't enter a seed. Move funds to a new
wallet bought direct from Ledger, with a new seed.

16
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:55,840
Center of mass at home: ruler on two tared mg scales,
wallet centred, read left (L) and right (R).

17
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:00,840
Rotate 180° and read again. Half the difference
cancels your placement error.

18
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,330
Type L and R.

19
00:01:03,530 --> 00:01:06,140
Rotate 180°, type the second L and R.

20
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:09,140
Offset −0.28 mm. About 1 mm of placement error cancelled.

21
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:12,140
Under the 0.7 mm example tolerance → normal. LIKELY GENUINE.

22
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:16,970
Implant unit: both pairs of readings.

23
00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:19,970
Offset +0.85 mm toward the right end.

24
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:23,470
Past 0.7 mm → CoM flagged. With +1.2 g → TAMPERED.

25
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:26,470
Yellow dot shifted (×5) toward the red end.

26
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:30,970
Until verified, keep it in a Faraday bag.
Test the bag: call a phone inside it.
